From: JoeyWu-tech
Subject: [PATCH] agent: a stopped distro's Hermes profiles are never listed

Upstream fix for #3924 (commit 97ca0160 on main 7f0f71a0). The Hermes
builder adds a field for each profile besides the connected one
(hermesProfileFields), found through hermesOthers and hermesProfiles,
which lists <root>/profiles and stats each profile's tombstone and
config.yaml. The builder runs at a stopped distro's place too, so every
build opened the distro's folder and started the distro again.

---
 internal/agent/hermes.go | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/internal/agent/hermes.go b/internal/agent/hermes.go
--- a/internal/agent/hermes.go
+++ b/internal/agent/hermes.go
@@ -342,7 +342,12 @@ var hermesProfileID = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`)
 // HERMES_HOME under it is a profile of; a HERMES_HOME elsewhere is the root itself, or, as
 // <root>/profiles/<name>, a profile of <root> (get_default_hermes_root).
 // A profile with no config.yaml yet is left out: magpie doesn't make one.
+// None at a stopped distro's place, whose folder is never listed: that
+// starts it (#3896).
 func hermesProfiles(at place) []string {
+	if at.cold {
+		return nil
+	}
 	root := hermesRoot(at)
 	paths := []string{filepath.Join(root, "config.yaml")}
 	ps := filepath.Join(root, "profiles")
